1:/// The terminal CLI core: a REPL that wires an [Agent] with the built-in
2:/// tools, streams events to the user, persists sessions, and compacts
3:/// context — all behind the injectable [CliIO] abstraction so it is fully
4:/// testable without a real terminal.
6:/// Shaped after pi-mono's coding-agent REPL (`packages/coding-agent/src/
7:/// cli` + `modes`), reduced to a plain line-based interface: assistant text
8:/// streams live, tool executions render as one-liners, and slash commands
9:/// (`/exit`, `/reset`, `/compact`, `/stats`, `/model`, `/help`) manage the
10:/// session. While a run is streaming, typed input is steered into the agent
11:/// (pi's first-class steering), and [CliIO.interrupts] abort it.
13:/// The real terminal wiring (stdin/stdout, SIGINT) lives in `bin/fah.dart`;
14:/// this library stays pure Dart.
